ely means not linked to any candidate. Since we have candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha, operator_available driver_operator_alpha is false. So we cannot assign to shift_candidate_beta unless we release first. But then we lose link needed for operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha. However maybe we can reassign after achieving operator_alignment_confirmed? Actually operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha is a goal; after achieving it we could release operator and then assign to shift_candidate_beta. But goal also requires candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha. So we need link after release. So we need to: achieve operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha (which needs constraint_applied and candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha). Then release operator from shift_candidate_alpha (making it available). Then assign operator to shift_candidate_beta. Then we still have operator_alignment_confirmed shift_candidate_alpha? Releasing operator does not affect operator_alignment_confirmed (it's a separate predicate). So we can keep that true. Good.

